From: Joan Karadimov <joan.karadimov@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Find our own executable without /proc

isOctoToolRunning() read /proc/self/exe through readlink(). QCoreApplication
::applicationFilePath() answers the same question, on every platform, and is
what /proc/self/exe resolves to on Linux -- so the non-Windows path is
unchanged in behaviour.

The /usr/bin comparison itself is skipped on Windows. That gate exists so the
setuid-root helper can trust the parent that invoked it -- hence octphelper's
own "Suspicious execution method" -- and that helper is not built here. There
is nothing left for it to protect, and /usr/bin is not where a mingw package
installs anything.

The readlink half is worth sending upstream. The gate half is not.
diff --git a/src/unixcommand.cpp b/src/unixcommand.cpp
index a696aad..caaf105 100644
--- a/src/unixcommand.cpp
+++ b/src/unixcommand.cpp
@@ -30,6 +30,7 @@
 #include <QRegularExpression>
 #include <QFile>
 #include <QFileInfo>
+#include <QCoreApplication>
 #include <QByteArray>
 #include <QTextStream>
 #include <QtNetwork>
@@ -1222,19 +1223,22 @@ bool UnixCommand::isAppRunning(const QString &appName, bool justOneInstance)
  * Checks if Octopi/Octopi-notifier, cache-cleaner, etc is being executed from /usr/bin
  */
 bool UnixCommand::isOctoToolRunning(const QString &octoToolName)
-{  
-  char exePath[PATH_MAX];
-  ssize_t count = readlink("/proc/self/exe", exePath, sizeof(exePath));
-  if (count == -1)
-  {
-    //perror("readlink");
-    return false;
-  }
-
-  QString path = QString::fromUtf8(exePath, count);
-  QFileInfo fi(path);
+{
+#ifdef Q_OS_WIN
+  // This gate exists so that the setuid-root helper can trust the parent that
+  // invoked it -- hence octphelper's own "Suspicious execution method". That
+  // helper is not built here (see the top-level CMakeLists), so there is
+  // nothing left for the gate to protect, and /usr/bin is not where a mingw
+  // package installs anything.
+  Q_UNUSED(octoToolName)
+  return true;
+#else
+  // QCoreApplication answers this without /proc, and gives the same path
+  // readlink("/proc/self/exe") did.
+  QFileInfo fi(QCoreApplication::applicationFilePath());
 
   return (fi.absoluteFilePath() == QLatin1String("/usr/bin/") + octoToolName);
+#endif
 }
 
